    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = x+yx^{5}, \left(2,-4\right), \left(-2,-4\right), \left(-4,-1\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,-4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-2,-4\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-4,-1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-126</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>126</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1020</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(2,-4\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(2,-4) = 2   - 4(2)^{5} = -126</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-2,-4\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-2,-4) = -2   - 4(-2)^{5} = 126</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-4,-1\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-4,-1) = -4   - 1(-4)^{5} = 1020</m>.


</solution>
